    "license": "Original project-authored parametric geometry and design. No external model, texture or generated image. Three.js 0.187.0 GLTFExporter and GLTFLoader are MIT licensed, copyright 2010–2026 three.js authors, retained in the pinned local LICENSE.",
    "prompt": "Purpose: four project-authored wall-mounted mirrors with distinct real mirror contours and solid frame geometry. Specification: fixed installation envelope 0.80m x 1.80m x 0.04m, metres, +Y up, +Z forward, centred wall-contact back at z=0 and identity scale. Functional contract: single planar-mirror-v1 / single-512-v1 reflective face at local z=0.026, node mirror-surface and no lights, occupancy, clock, information or use points. Geometry: finite convex counterclockwise polygons, one coplanar face mesh, complete positive-Z triangulation, closed thick back and closed frames wholly outside declared mirror interiors. Budget: deterministic CPU polygon geometry and Three.js GLB export with CPU GLTFLoader readback, no online dependency and no raster reflection baked into assets. Editable source: per-design contour sampling, frame width, color and surface parameters. Export and provenance: exact source, contract, generator and dependency SHA256 pins. Static GLB mirror face is an inspection surface. Actual host scene reflection is supplied only by the separately verified runtime binding. Design: A .68m wide and 1.68m high mirror with straight lower sides, a true semicircular top sampled in 48 equal angular segments, and a continuous brown solid offset arch frame.",
    "sourceDesign": "arch",
    "method": "Project-authored deterministic CPU convex polygon triangulation, solid offset ring frames, solid backing and solid mullions. GLB contains static inspection geometry. Runtime binds the actual host-scene Reflector separately."
